## How to Treat Toenail Fungus: Your Options Explained

What actually works, and does it depend on how bad things have gotten? Both questions deserve a straight answer, because the treatment that suits a faint white patch is rarely the one that suits a fully thickened, separated nail.

Oral terbinafine is currently the most effective treatment for <strong>toenail fungus</strong>, with the highest cure rates among available options, and that single fact should shape how you think about your choices. It works by circulating through the bloodstream and reaching the nail from underneath as it grows, rather than trying to fight through the nail plate from above, which is the central limitation every topical product runs into.

<strong>Terbinafine</strong> is an oral antifungal medication taken daily, usually for around six to twelve weeks, with the highest clinical cure rates for onychomycosis among available treatments. Because it is processed by the liver, doctors typically order liver function blood tests beforehand and sometimes again partway through, particularly if you take other medications or have existing liver concerns. This is the detail that makes people hesitate, understandably, but for most healthy adults the monitoring is routine rather than alarming.

For milder, earlier-stage infections, topical options are reasonable first steps. Antifungal nail lacquers and creams containing ingredients like ciclopirox can clear surface-level infections, particularly white superficial onychomycosis, though they need months of consistent daily use and cannot reliably reach deeper infection. If you would rather start at home before involving a prescription, our guide on <a href='/blog/toenail-fungus/toenail-fungus-home-remedies'>home remedies for toenail fungus</a> covers what genuinely has some evidence behind it and what is mostly folklore.

Laser therapy sits in a slightly different category. It can temporarily improve the appearance of the nail, but <a href='https://www.scripps.org/news_items/7235-which-toenail-fungus-treatment-is-best'>Scripps Health</a> notes it has a lower cure rate than oral medication, making it a reasonable option for people who cannot take oral antifungals rather than a default first choice. Sessions are quick and largely painless, but expect to budget for more than one, and for full detail including <strong>laser treatment for toenail fungus cost</strong>, our dedicated comparison breaks down what clinics typically charge.

So which path fits you? Mild, surface-only discolouration with no thickening generally warrants a topical attempt first. Moderate thickening, multiple affected nails, or a history of failed topical treatment points toward oral terbinafine. Severe cases with significant pain, deformity, or diabetes in the picture warrant a prescriber's involvement from the start rather than working through tiers. For a full comparison across every tier, see our breakdown of the <a href='/blog/toenail-fungus/best-toenail-fungus-treatment'>best toenail fungus treatment</a> options.

