## Why Does Toenail Fungus Take So Long to Clear?

Why does a course of pills that lasts a matter of weeks take the better part of a year to show real results? The pill is not the slow part. Your nail is.

It typically takes six to eighteen months depending on treatment type and infection severity, and the timeline comes down to nail growth rate rather than how the medication works. Terbinafine kills the active fungus within weeks. What you are waiting on after that is the nail itself growing out clean.

Toenails grow at roughly a millimetre a month, slower than fingernails and slower still in older adults. A medication can eliminate the infection completely, yet the visible nail, already damaged and discoloured from months of fungal activity, has to be pushed out entirely by new growth at the base before the toe looks normal again. On a big toe, full replacement can take the better part of a year, sometimes longer. This is the single most common source of frustration in treatment, and it is also entirely normal. A clear nail at the cuticle within a few months is the actual sign treatment is working, even while the tip still looks rough.

