## Living With Clearer Nails

A discoloured, thickened toenail is not a verdict on your hygiene, and it is not something you caused through carelessness. It is a common infection with a known biology, a real timeline, and treatment options that genuinely work when matched to severity.

What we would push back on is the instinct to wait it out indefinitely, hoping a problem that almost never resolves on its own will somehow be the exception. Get the diagnosis confirmed if there is any doubt, particularly if psoriasis or trauma is plausible. Choose treatment based on where you actually are, not the most aggressive option or the gentlest one by default. And give the nail the months it genuinely needs to grow out, because patience here is not optional, it is the actual mechanism of recovery. Clear nails are achievable. They just take the right plan and the time biology demands, nothing more dramatic than that.
